  "result": "Done! I've implemented credit note functionality:\n\n**Added `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` in src/credits.js:**\n- Creates credit notes for refunds on issued, partially_paid, or paid invoices\n- Returns `ok(creditNote)` with { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n- **Number format:** CN-YYYY-NNNN (separate counter per year, independent of invoice numbers)\n- **Validation:**\n  - Invoice must not be draft (NOT_ISSUED)\n  - Date must be YYYY-MM-DD format (DATE_INVALID)\n  - Amount must be positive integer in cents (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Amount cannot exceed invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n\n**Extended src/numbering.js:**\n- Added `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` for CN- prefixed numbers\n- Supports mixed INV- and CN- numbers in existingNumbers\n\n**Added error code:** CREDIT_TOO_HIGH\n\n**Added 15 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Successful credit note creation on issued invoices\n- Works on partially_paid and paid invoices (not just issued)\n- NOT_ISSUED error for draft invoices\n- Amount validation (non-integer, zero, negative)\n- CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error when exceeding total\n- Amount equal to invoice total (allowed)\n- Date validation\n- CN- number format and incrementing\n- Counter reset per year\n- Input immutability\n- Return structure\n\nAll 204 tests pass \u2713 (189 existing + 15 new credit note tests)",
